<wpt lat="45.260000" lon="-121.621200"><ele>988.7</ele><name>Road 3530-011 below the Mineral Creek confluence</name><desc>source: USFS EDW road 3530011 vertex on the west bank, just below where Mineral Creek joins the White River; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 187</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.232300" lon="-121.625700"><ele>934.3</ele><name>Road 3530-011 / Barlow Road junction, by Barlow Creek Campground</name><desc>source: USFS EDW 3530011 south end on Road 3530, 1 mi above Barlow Crossing; DEM 3,065 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 187; book_elev_ft: 3000; quote: they join at Barlow Crossing about 8 miles to the east and 1,300 feet lower</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.272000" lon="-121.681100"><ele>1138.3</ele><name>Devils Half Acre</name><desc>source: USFS EDW 3530000 / Devils Half Acre trailhead (OSM node 33441317); confidence: high; pdf_page: 178; quote: descend Road 3530 in a southeasterly direction for 1 mile to Devils Half Acre</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.280930" lon="-121.684000"><ele>1247.4</ele><name>Mineral Jane Trail junction on Road 3530</name><desc>source: OSM west end of Barlow Butte Trail #670 (alt_name Mineral Jane Ski Trail, way 548899768); confidence: high; pdf_page: 179; quote: From Barlow Pass Sno-Park descend the Devils Half Acre Trail 250 yards, then turn left onto the Mineral Jane Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.281801" lon="-121.675262"><ele>1256.5</ele><name>Mineral Jane Ski Trail east end</name><desc>source: OSM way 548899767 east end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 180</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.284048" lon="-121.670152"><ele>1228.1</ele><name>Barlow Saddle</name><desc>source: OSM south end of 3560-220 by Road 3560 at Highway 35; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 180; book_elev_ft: 4000; quote: a series of clearcuts and road that leads to Barlow Saddle 0.9 mile from Barlow Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.296900" lon="-121.675000"><ele>1259.2</ele><name>Road 3560-220 north end</name><desc>source: USFS EDW 3560220 end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 180; quote: From Barlow Saddle the trail follows a road through a clearcut, then leaves the road to cross Mineral Creek</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.302200" lon="-121.671200"><ele>1287.7</ele><name>Mineral Jane trailhead at the bridge</name><desc>source: as above; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 180; quote: then climbs gently to the highway bridge at White River opposite White River West Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.303657" lon="-121.674434"><ele>1305.0</ele><name>White River West Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high</desc></wpt>
